# Veggie Couscous with Spicy Pine Nuts

Based on [Chrissy Teigen Cravings](https://www.penguinrandomhouse.com/books/252973/cravings-by-chrissy-teigen-with-adeena-sussman/) ([wayback](http://web.archive.org/web/20251202235345/https://www.penguinrandomhouse.com/books/252973/cravings-by-chrissy-teigen-with-adeena-sussman/)), pg. 193

{ rating="4" image="veggie_couscous_with_spicy_pine_nuts.jpeg" }
:::
:::

## Ingredients

### For the Vegetables

- [ ] 3 Tbsp [olive oil]{ ing="olive-oil" } (plus more for drizzling)
- [ ] 1 large [onion]{ ing="onion" }, chopped
- [ ] 1.5 tsp [kosher salt]{ ing="kosher-salt" }
- [ ] 1/2 tsp [ground cinnamon]{ ing="ground-cinnamon" }
- [ ] 1/2 tsp [ground cumin]{ ing="ground-cumin" } (or 1/4 tsp coriander)
- [ ] 1/4 tsp [cayenne pepper]{ ing="cayenne-pepper" }
- [ ] 1 lb [sweet potato]{ ing="sweet-potato" }, peeled and cut into 1.5 in chunks
- [ ] 1 lb [zucchini]{ ing="zucchini" }, cut into 2 in chunks
- [ ] 1.5 cups [vegetable]{ ing="vegetable" } (or chicken) broth
- [ ] [cilantro garnish]{ ing="cilantro-garnish" }, optional

### Couscous

- [ ] Prep the couscous [following package instructions]{ ing="following-package-instructions" }
- [ ] [If regular couscous]{ ing="if-regular-couscous" }, add 1/3 cup sliced almonds

_Note: we couldn’t find pine nuts, so we used a pine nut boxed couscous.
For the full recipe with the nuts, see the cookbook!_

## Recipe

1. Chop and prep the [vegetables]{ ing="vegetable" }
1. In the dutch oven, heat the [olive oil]{ ing="olive-oil" } over medium heat
1. Cook the [onion]{ ing="onion" } until tender (7 min), then add the [cinnamon]{ ing="ground-cinnamon" }, [cumin]{ ing="ground-cumin" }, cayenne, and [salt]{ ing="kosher-salt" } (1 min)
1. Add the [sweet potato]{ ing="sweet-potato" }, [zucchini]{ ing="zucchini" }, and broth
1. _Meanwhile_ start the [couscous]{ ing="if-regular-couscous" } following the box directions
1. Bring to a boil then reduce heat to a simmer and cook until the sweet potatoes are easily pierced with a fork (15-20 min)
1. Serve the vegetables over the fluffed couscous. Season with salt and [pepper]{ ing="cayenne-pepper" }, and drizzle with olive oil, and optionally [garnish]{ ing="cilantro-garnish" } with cilantro
